{
  "id": "xjmUzxEPJeM",
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 3.9,
      "end": 21.82,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "For the last 20 years, I've interviewed hundreds of people about their motivation to create, their ambition and what it feels like to be whole and at home in the world on my podcast, \"Design Matters.\"",
          "start": 3.9,
          "end": 21.82
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "ambition",
          "ko": "야망, 포부",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "term": "whole and at home in the world",
          "ko": "온전하고 세상에 편안히 속한",
          "type": "phrase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 23.32,
      "end": 34.9,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "In one episode several years ago, I interviewed a famous painter about a recent exhibition, a show that had taken years to create.",
          "start": 23.32,
          "end": 34.9
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "exhibition",
          "ko": "전시회",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 35.87,
      "end": 52.85,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Given the magnitude of the accomplishment, I asked her how long the feeling of pride lasted after opening night.",
          "start": 35.87,
          "end": 44.48
        },
        {
          "text": "She looked at me, she smiled sheepishly and stated, \"About 11 minutes.\"",
          "start": 45.28,
          "end": 52.85
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "given the magnitude",
          "ko": "그 엄청난 규모를 감안하면",
          "type": "phrase"
        },
        {
          "term": "accomplishment",
          "ko": "성취, 업적",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "term": "sheepishly",
          "ko": "멋쩍게, 쑥스럽게",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 54.25,
      "end": 66.83,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "I thought she was joking, but she wasn't.",
          "start": 54.25,
          "end": 57.46
        },
        {
          "text": "Since that interview, I've come to realize she's not the only one whose achievements feel ephemeral and fleeting.",
          "start": 57.99,
          "end": 66.83
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "come to realize",
          "ko": "차츰 깨닫게 되다",
          "type": "phrase"
        },
        {
          "term": "ephemeral and fleeting",
          "ko": "덧없고 순식간에 사라지는",
          "type": "phrase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 67.47,
      "end": 78.24,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Not by a long shot.",
          "start": 67.47,
          "end": 69.07
        },
        {
          "text": "Over the past four years, in addition to my interviews, I've conducted my own version of a Proustian questionnaire for PRINT magazine.",
          "start": 69.83,
          "end": 78.24
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "not by a long shot",
          "ko": "전혀 그렇지 않다",
          "type": "idiom"
        },
        {
          "term": "conducted",
          "ko": "(조사를) 실시하다, 수행하다",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "term": "questionnaire",
          "ko": "설문지",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 78.74,
      "end": 86.25,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Hundreds of creative people have answered the same 10 questions about their life and their work.",
          "start": 78.74,
          "end": 86.25
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 86.92,
      "end": 100.5,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Given the response I had with the famous painter, I included this question: How long does the feeling of pride and joy at accomplishing something last for you?",
          "start": 86.92,
          "end": 100.5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 102.5,
      "end": 124.05,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "As I collected my responses to the questionnaire and reviewed all of my transcripts of my interviews and conversations, I saw how, up close, for so many people, the pride and joy of accomplishment dissipates almost as quickly as it manifests.",
          "start": 102.5,
          "end": 124.05
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "transcripts",
          "ko": "글로 옮긴 기록, 녹취록",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "term": "up close",
          "ko": "가까이서, 면밀히",
          "type": "phrase"
        },
        {
          "term": "dissipates",
          "ko": "흩어져 사라지다",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "term": "manifests",
          "ko": "겉으로 나타나다",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 124.76,
      "end": 141.41,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "I heard it in the words of a poet who shared that the high of publishing a book lasted until she sent in her final manuscript.",
          "start": 124.76,
          "end": 133.73
        },
        {
          "text": "I heard it in the voice of a designer who admitted he felt restless the very night of an awards ceremony.",
          "start": 133.76,
          "end": 141.41
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "the high of",
          "ko": "~이 주는 짜릿한 들뜸",
          "type": "phrase"
        },
        {
          "term": "manuscript",
          "ko": "(책의) 원고",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "term": "restless",
          "ko": "안절부절못하는",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 141.81,
      "end": 156.49,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "And I heard it in the plaintiff confession of a musician who told me, \"The only time I feel at peace is when I'm in the studio.",
          "start": 141.81,
          "end": 153.38
        },
        {
          "text": "Not on stage, not after.",
          "start": 153.42,
          "end": 156.49
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "plaintive confession",
          "ko": "애처로운 고백",
          "type": "phrase"
        },
        {
          "term": "at peace",
          "ko": "마음이 평온한",
          "type": "phrase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 156.52,
      "end": 162.09,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Only while I'm making.\"",
          "start": 156.52,
          "end": 159.29
        },
        {
          "text": "Another confession.",
          "start": 160.59,
          "end": 162.09
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 163.36,
      "end": 179.68,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "I felt this way my whole life.",
          "start": 163.36,
          "end": 165.8
        },
        {
          "text": "After publishing a book, after mounting an exhibition, after a TED Talk, after what should feel like I've reached the pinnacle, moments I've dreamed of for decades.",
          "start": 166.13,
          "end": 179.68
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "mounting an exhibition",
          "ko": "전시회를 열다, 준비하다",
          "type": "phrase"
        },
        {
          "term": "pinnacle",
          "ko": "정점, 절정",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 179.68,
      "end": 194.19,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "The joy evaporates within days, sometimes hours, and once, terrifyingly, within minutes.",
          "start": 179.68,
          "end": 188.82
        },
        {
          "text": "And then for so many people, what happens next?",
          "start": 189.92,
          "end": 194.19
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "evaporates",
          "ko": "증발하듯 사라지다",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 194.59,
      "end": 212.38,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "The quest to create, to make something bigger, more ambitious or more challenging begins again.",
          "start": 194.59,
          "end": 203.33
        },
        {
          "text": "I found this all utterly confounding, and I became consumed with the question of why?",
          "start": 205.17,
          "end": 212.38
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "quest",
          "ko": "탐구, 갈망",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "term": "utterly",
          "ko": "완전히, 철저히",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "term": "confounding",
          "ko": "어리둥절하게 하는, 당혹스러운",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "term": "consumed with",
          "ko": "~에 완전히 사로잡힌",
          "type": "phrase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 212.41,
      "end": 222.85,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Why does the feeling of creative achievement slip away almost as soon as we grasp it?",
          "start": 212.41,
          "end": 218.95
        },
        {
          "text": "Why are we in such a rush to want something more?",
          "start": 218.98,
          "end": 222.85
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "slip away",
          "ko": "슬며시 사라지다, 빠져나가다",
          "type": "phrase"
        },
        {
          "term": "grasp",
          "ko": "움켜쥐다, 붙잡다",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 222.89,
      "end": 242.14,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Is it ego, ambition, addiction to attainment?",
          "start": 222.89,
          "end": 228.09
        },
        {
          "text": "We're living in a culture now obsessed with achievement, and we measure that success with metrics, likes, views, followers, awards, trophies, sales and we celebrate the hustle.",
          "start": 228.86,
          "end": 242.14
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "addiction to attainment",
          "ko": "성취에 대한 중독",
          "type": "phrase"
        },
        {
          "term": "obsessed with",
          "ko": "~에 집착하는",
          "type": "phrase"
        },
        {
          "term": "the hustle",
          "ko": "치열하게 노력하는 것, 분주함",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 242.17,
      "end": 257.79,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "We glorify the grind, and we equate visibility with value.",
          "start": 242.17,
          "end": 248.18
        },
        {
          "text": "Now after 20 years of interviewing more than 1,000 people, I've come to believe that something else is at play.",
          "start": 249.01,
          "end": 257.79
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "glorify the grind",
          "ko": "고된 노력 자체를 미화하다",
          "type": "phrase"
        },
        {
          "term": "equate ... with",
          "ko": "~을 ~와 동일시하다",
          "type": "phrase"
        },
        {
          "term": "at play",
          "ko": "작용하고 있는",
          "type": "idiom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 258.99,
      "end": 272.17,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "When I look at the creative people I admire most, I see people answering a calling.",
          "start": 258.99,
          "end": 266.86
        },
        {
          "text": "A calling that says create, shape, build, imagine, express.",
          "start": 267.3,
          "end": 272.17
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "admire",
          "ko": "존경하다, 동경하다",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "term": "answering a calling",
          "ko": "소명에 응답하다",
          "type": "idiom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 272.47,
      "end": 284.25,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Not necessarily to be seen, but to be.",
          "start": 272.47,
          "end": 277.04
        },
        {
          "text": "What if the actual reward is not accomplishment but the act of creating?",
          "start": 277.57,
          "end": 284.25
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "not necessarily",
          "ko": "반드시 ~인 것은 아닌",
          "type": "phrase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 284.88,
      "end": 292.76,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Think about it.",
          "start": 284.88,
          "end": 286.12
        },
        {
          "text": "The finished products and trappings of creative accomplishment are often seen as the goal.",
          "start": 286.15,
          "end": 292.76
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "trappings",
          "ko": "겉으로 드러나는 부속물, 겉치레",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 292.79,
      "end": 300.63,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "And if we haven't yet reached mastery, we're told we have to fake it until we make it.",
          "start": 292.79,
          "end": 299.1
        },
        {
          "text": "Pretend.",
          "start": 299.5,
          "end": 300.63
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "mastery",
          "ko": "숙달, 통달",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "term": "fake it until you make it",
          "ko": "될 때까지 ~인 척하라",
          "type": "idiom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 301.73,
      "end": 309.27,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "But I don't think people should have to fake anything.",
          "start": 301.73,
          "end": 304.54
        },
        {
          "text": "Instead, I'd rather make it until I make it.",
          "start": 305.04,
          "end": 309.27
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 310.54,
      "end": 319.98,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "You see, I believe that the act of making is like oxygen.",
          "start": 310.54,
          "end": 315.81
        },
        {
          "text": "When the making stops, it becomes hard to breathe.",
          "start": 316.31,
          "end": 319.98
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 321.08,
      "end": 335.13,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Now I admit I still struggle with this.",
          "start": 321.08,
          "end": 324.05
        },
        {
          "text": "I crave recognition, I still measure myself by external markers of success, and I'm still racing towards multiple finish lines.",
          "start": 324.05,
          "end": 335.13
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "crave",
          "ko": "갈망하다, 몹시 원하다",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "term": "recognition",
          "ko": "인정, 알아봐 줌",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 335.53,
      "end": 350.95,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "But I'm learning, albeit slowly, that these moments will never, ever be enough.",
          "start": 335.53,
          "end": 341.87
        },
        {
          "text": "They can't be, because in the end, they represent a certain scarcity, while making is the actual abundance.",
          "start": 341.91,
          "end": 350.95
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "albeit",
          "ko": "비록 ~이긴 하지만",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "term": "scarcity",
          "ko": "결핍, 부족함",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "term": "abundance",
          "ko": "풍요로움",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 352.22,
      "end": 371.34,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Several years ago, I interviewed David Lee Roth, the swashbuckling former frontman of the rock group Van Halen.",
          "start": 352.22,
          "end": 361.89
        },
        {
          "text": "I first became a fan of the band in the mid-1980s, after the release of their five-time platinum album, \"1984.\"",
          "start": 361.93,
          "end": 371.34
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "swashbuckling",
          "ko": "호탕하고 거침없는",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "term": "frontman",
          "ko": "(밴드의) 리드 보컬, 간판 멤버",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 371.34,
      "end": 384.92,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "The record sold over 12 million copies, produced four singles, peaked at number two on the Billboard charts, and was only held back from the number one position by Michael Jackson's \"Thriller.\"",
          "start": 371.34,
          "end": 384.92
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "peaked at",
          "ko": "최고 ~위에 오르다",
          "type": "phrase"
        },
        {
          "term": "held back",
          "ko": "가로막히다, 저지되다",
          "type": "phrase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 386.22,
      "end": 403.03,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "I interviewed David Lee in 2019 and asked him what it felt like to reach the peak of the tallest mountain in his storied career.",
          "start": 386.22,
          "end": 398
        },
        {
          "text": "He paused and was reflective as he recalled the experience.",
          "start": 398.93,
          "end": 403.03
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "storied",
          "ko": "유서 깊은, 화려한 이력의",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "term": "reflective",
          "ko": "사색에 잠긴",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "term": "recalled",
          "ko": "회상하다, 떠올리다",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 403.07,
      "end": 420.32,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "And what he said next really surprised me.",
          "start": 403.07,
          "end": 406.47
        },
        {
          "text": "He told me you have to be really careful when you reach that peak, as it's always cold, you’re often alone, and there's only one direction to go.",
          "start": 407.3,
          "end": 420.32
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 420.95,
      "end": 439.6,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "And it occurred to me right then and there that I didn't want to peak until the day before I die.",
          "start": 420.95,
          "end": 427.02
        },
        {
          "text": "And I wanted to take my time, slowly, walking up that mountain, making new things all along the way.",
          "start": 429.16,
          "end": 439.6
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "it occurred to me",
          "ko": "문득 ~라는 생각이 들었다",
          "type": "idiom"
        },
        {
          "term": "right then and there",
          "ko": "바로 그 자리에서",
          "type": "idiom"
        },
        {
          "term": "take my time",
          "ko": "천천히 하다, 서두르지 않다",
          "type": "idiom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 440.57,
      "end": 452.85,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "So the next time you finish anything, a book, a poem, a song, a painting, try not to despair.",
          "start": 440.57,
          "end": 447.95
        },
        {
          "text": "That fleeting feeling of accomplishment isn't a flaw.",
          "start": 448.28,
          "end": 452.85
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "despair",
          "ko": "절망하다",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "term": "flaw",
          "ko": "결함, 흠",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 453.52,
      "end": 458.42,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "It's part of the creative condition.",
          "start": 453.52,
          "end": 455.52
        },
        {
          "text": "Instead, heed the calling.",
          "start": 455.82,
          "end": 458.42
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "heed the calling",
          "ko": "소명에 귀 기울이다",
          "type": "phrase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 458.46,
      "end": 470.63,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Continue to make things, and maybe, just maybe, take your time becoming the creative being that you want to be.",
          "start": 458.46,
          "end": 468.8
        },
        {
          "text": "Thank you.",
          "start": 469.5,
          "end": 470.63
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
